{"term":"Indian","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:bf0711c3cbf9db48ee","definition":"Of or relating to India or its people; or (formerly) of the East Indies.","example":"An IAF representative told an Indian parliamentary committee that due to the Ukraine war a “major delivery” from Moscow “is not going to take place.”","pos":"adj","synonyms":["East Indian","Indic","Hindian","Desi","Indish"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Indian#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:14afa686a9b67cda34","definition":"Eastern; Oriental.","example":"The morrow next apprear'd with purple hayre / Yet dropping fresh out of the Indian fount, / And bringing light into the heavens fayre […].","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Indian#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c1dc85e263240d7b0d","definition":"Of or relating to the indigenous peoples of the Americas.","example":"The hardships of bark-collecting in the primeval forests of South America are of the severest kind, and undergone only by the half-civilized Indians and people of mixed race, in the pay of speculators or companies located in the towns.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["Native American","Amerindian","First Nation"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"proscribed","register":"proscribed","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Indian#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e3805b1ff136278a02","definition":"Made with Indian corn or maize.","example":"Indian bread","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Canada, US, proscribed","register":"Canada, US, proscribed","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Indian#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:08c36e80c6c8fd5a76","definition":"Designating any of various chess openings now characterised by black's attempt to control the board through knights and fianchettoed bishops rather than with a central pawn advance.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Indian#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e99acdb0f87ee84e08","definition":"A person from India.","example":"[A]ll personnel are to be hereby ordered to refer to her as a \"Kumiho,\" and not a \"Kitsune.\" Personnel asking what the difference is are to be reminded of the difference between a Cherokee Indian and a New Delhi Indian.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["Asian Indian","East Indian","Hindian","Desi"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["honest Indian","Pueblo Indian"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Indian#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a139c6ad51c87e4710","definition":"An American Indian, a member of one of the indigenous peoples of the Americas (generally excluding the Aleut, Inuit, Metis, and Yupik).","example":"We stigmatize the Indians, also, as cowardly and treacherous, because they use stratagem in warfare in preference to open force; but in this they are fully justified by their rude code of honor.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["Amerindian","Native American","Red Indian","First Nations person","American Indian","Amerind","Amerindian","First A